---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const principles = [
  ['Open by default', 'Knowledge compounds when others can inspect, reuse and challenge it. Closed work should require a reason, not openness.'],
  ['Publish to establish provenance', 'Early public disclosure creates a timestamped intellectual record and makes ideas available for criticism and reuse.'],
  ['Version instead of waiting for finality', 'Research is allowed to improve in public. Every release should state what is claim, evidence, conjecture and revision.'],
  ['Treat attention as a scarce resource', 'Abundant output can still impoverish a system if it consumes more human attention than the value it creates.'],
  ['Prefer selection quality over generation volume', 'The objective is not to maximise the number of ideas. It is to improve the rate at which valuable possibilities are recognised and realised.'],
  ['Build demonstrations, not only arguments', 'Software, models and reproducible analyses are part of the research programme because they force conceptual claims into contact with constraints.'],
  ['Use exclusivity only when it enables realisation', 'Patenting is an instrument, not a default. It is justified only when temporary exclusivity is plausibly necessary to finance, coordinate or protect the difficult work of turning an idea into a socially useful reality.'],
  ['Keep institutions provisional', 'Agalmic Research should be judged by the quality, openness and durability of its work, not by whether it prematurely imitates the bureaucracy of an established institute.'],
];
---
<Layout title="Principles" description="Operating principles for Agalmic Research: open publication, provenance, versioning, attention discipline and selective use of intellectual property.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Principles</p>
      <h1>The institution should embody the thesis.</h1>
      <p class="lede">If the research argues that knowledge can become abundant, the research practice itself should make knowledge cheap to access, inspect, reproduce and extend.</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="grid">
        {principles.map(([title, copy], i) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class="card-kicker">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <h3>{title}</h3>
            <p>{copy}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A useful default</p>
        <h2>Publish first. Publish clearly. Keep improving.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p class="large">“Publish immediately” is a strong default, not a commandment.</p>
        <p class="muted">The exception is when disclosure would destroy the ability to realise an invention whose implementation genuinely requires protected capital, coordination or regulatory investment. The burden of proof sits with secrecy, not with publication.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
